 ## Consent presets
 
+### How presets are built
+
+Presets are **derived from `TOOL_SCOPE_MAP`** in `src/auth/scopes.ts`, not hand-listed:
+
+- **Read only** = the `.read` form of every scope any tool needs.
+- **Read + write** = every write scope any tool needs, plus the read scope of families that have no write tool (settings, reports). A `.read` scope whose write parent is requested is omitted because a Xero write scope includes read.
+
+Consequences enforced by `npm test`:
+
+- every implemented tool is registered under **Read + write**;
+- no scope is requested that no tool uses (so no `accounting.settings` write, no `accounting.reports.taxreports.read`);
+- **Read only** never contains a write scope.
+
+The consent page shows the exact scope list under each option.
+
