+## Xero app configuration
+
+Xero only issues scopes that are enabled on the app in the [developer portal](https://developer.xero.com/app/manage). Every scope in the **Read + write** list above must be ticked on the app, or Xero rejects the authorisation with `invalid_scope`. Enabling a scope on the app does not grant it: the user still has to consent at Xero.
+
+## Changing scopes on an existing connection
+
+A scope change never widens an existing grant. After deploying a scope change:
+
+1. In the MCP client (Claude, ChatGPT, Inspector), disconnect / remove the server and add it again.
+2. On the consent page choose **Read + write**, then approve at Xero.
+3. Call `list_granted_scopes`: it lists `available_tools` and `unavailable_tools` with the scope each hidden tool needs.
+
+An old MCP session keeps the scope set it was issued with until the client reconnects; tools are registered once per session from that set.
+
 ## Override
 
-Advanced deploys may set secret/env `XERO_SCOPES_OVERRIDE` (space-separated) to replace the preset scope string. Prefer presets for least privilege.
+Advanced deploys may set secret/env `XERO_SCOPES_OVERRIDE` (space-separated) to replace the preset scope string for **both** presets. When it is set the consent page says so and shows the exact override, so a narrowed deployment cannot present itself as full read + write. Prefer presets for least privilege.
